---
title: "Installation"
description: "Install the Photon CLI with a package manager or as a standalone binary."
---

Photon CLI runs on **Node.js 22 or newer**. Node must be available on your
`PATH` regardless of which package manager installs the CLI.

## Install with a package manager

<CodeGroup>
```sh npm
npm install --global @photon-ai/cli
```

```sh pnpm
pnpm add --global @photon-ai/cli
```

```sh Yarn
yarn add --dev @photon-ai/cli
yarn photon --version
```

```sh Bun
bun add --global @photon-ai/cli
```
</CodeGroup>

Bun works as the package manager, but Node.js remains the supported runtime.

## Install a standalone binary

<Note>
  Standalone installers for macOS, Linux, and Windows are coming. Until they
  ship, install the CLI with a package manager.
</Note>

## Verify the install

```sh
photon --version
photon --help
```

